  99: ## T8 — Durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery
 100: Reasoning: The core of G1: write-before-dispatch, persistence across reload/close, ordered automatic drain 
meeting D1; unknown-outcome recovery follows in T27.
 101: Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, 
reply target, requested mention IDs, original send time, window start, order, state, generation) before dispatch and 
before the composer clears; pending items render with a text label; items drain automatically per conversation in 
order when connectivity returns, with ≤ 10 pending and quota available all delivered within 10 s; confirmed items 
become the normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 
behavior kept); if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay 
with the D5 message.
