  45: ## T28 — Membership integrity: memberships only through authorized server paths
  46: Reasoning: Every members-only guarantee of this phase (typing topic, mentions, roster, read state, messages, 
attachments, receipts) trusts `conversation_members`; owner decision D9 puts the self-enrolment gap in scope (PLAN 
review r4 #1–#3 widened it to every client-reachable and server-side path that creates or restores a membership).
  47: Task: A `conversation_members` row is created or restored only by a server path that authorizes that user for 
that conversation (direct conversation creation among the users it names, under the existing company rules; room 
conversation membership per the room's access rules; an explicitly authorized room join/rejoin; test seeding). No anon 
or authenticated client — acting through `conversation_members`, `conversations` INSERT/UPDATE (`participants`, 
`room_id`, `type`), the participant sync trigger `sync_conversation_members`, the conversation resolver/join routes, 
or any other RPC, view, or trigger — can make itself or any other user a member it is not authorized to be, or move a 
membership to another conversation or user. A removed membership stays removed when unrelated writes happen (another 
user's join, a participants sync, preference/archive/read writes); only an authorized rejoin restores it. Preference, 
archive, and read writes update an existing membership and never create one; a membership that vanished between 
authorization and the write is answered as not a participant with no row created. What a client DELETE of its own 
membership means (leave, or forbidden) is decided and recorded. The hosted build and the Phase 4 build keep creating 
direct and room conversations, joining rooms, and changing preferences/archive/read state (including their user-scoped 
writes, e.g. preference upserts of an existing membership). The inventory of membership writers and the decision for 
each is recorded in TRACK.
  48: Done when: On the local database, for each inventoried path, neither a hostile actor nor the user it targets 
gains or regains membership without authorization, and the legitimate creation, join, rejoin, preference, archive, and 
read flows of the current, Phase 4, and hosted builds still work.
  49: Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests (PostgREST as anon, as an authenticated outsider, and as a current 
member; real routes) asserting the complete membership delta and the affected users' access (403 on 
