 149: ## 9. Data and integrations
 150: 
 151: ### Data inputs
 152: - Composer text, reply target, and mention selections (user IDs).
 153: - Browser connectivity events, Realtime stream status, tab visibility, Supabase auth state changes.
 154: - Responses from `POST /api/messages/create` (status and error code) and from the fence/lookup call.
 155: 
 156: ### Data outputs
 157: - Browser IndexedDB outbox keyed by application user ID: `clientMessageId`, conversation ID, text, reply target, 
requested mention user IDs, pressed-send time, delivery-window start, order, state (waiting / claimed / unknown / 
failed + reason / expired), attempt generation, claim holder and lease expiry. Deleted per BR-007/BR-008; never shared 
across users.
 158: - Database: attempt-generation state per (sender, conversation, `clientMessageId`) so a fenced or stale 
generation cannot commit; the original submitted composition used for replay comparison; mention records written 
atomically with the message; private typing-topic authorization (RLS on `realtime.messages`, `users.supabase_uid = 
auth.uid()::text` → `users.id` membership); `mark_conversation_read` with an internal membership check; 
`get_unread_counts` without `anon` EXECUTE; rate-limit buckets for all create requests and for fence/lookup calls, 
separate from the insertion quota.
 159: - API: create route sender and attempt-generation fencing, winning-insert quota charging, request budget, 
`clientMessageId` in responses; fence/lookup route for the caller's own message only; authenticated, rate-limited, 
size-bounded metrics route.
 160: - Structured metric log lines (BR-013).
 161: - Persisted drawer state per user: open flag + active conversation ID.
 162: 
 163: ### Integrations
 164: - Supabase Postgres, Realtime (`postgres_changes`, private broadcast topics), Auth (server routes use 
`createSupabaseServerClient` + `auth.getUser()`).
 165: - Browser APIs: IndexedDB, Web Locks and/or BroadcastChannel for cross-tab claims and signals, Notification API 
(Phase 4), Page Visibility.
 166: - Hosting/Supabase logs as the metrics sink; no new external analytics dependency.
