indefinitely. [SPEC:96](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:96). **Fix:** 
require server-fenced attempt ownership and bounded recovery; unknown becomes waiting only when no previous attempt 
can still commit. Test with the original INSERT blocked in real Postgres through lookup, cancellation, and takeover. 
**r2 #2/#5 remain partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-4-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-5-2. **High — FR-001 versus §11/AC-039: 
IndexedDB failure bypasses durability.** The Phase 4 fallback permits dispatch without durable storage, reopening the 
original close-before-response loss window. Phase 4 keeps the key in a component ref and uses plain fetch 
([message-composer.tsx:145](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/message-composer.tsx:145), 
[messaging-api.ts:131](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging-api.ts:131)). 
[SPEC:196](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:196). **Fix:** “If the 
durable write fails, do not dispatch or clear the composer; retain the composition with an actionable storage 
failure.” AC-039 must inject storage failure with HTTP working and assert zero create requests. **r2 #1 remains 
partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-6-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md:7:3. **High — FR-024/025, §12, AC-024/026: 
send-time membership does not authorize later notification.** AC-024 tests someone already outside the conversation. 
It misses removal after commit but before enrichment/notification completes, and account switching during that wait. 
The existing handler already awaits a claim before displaying content 
([use-message-notifications.ts:124](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/ui/use-message-notifications.ts:124)). 
[SPEC:217](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:217). **Fix:** fence 
pending notifications by current identity and membership generation, require current authorization before emission, 
and discard work on removal/switch. Add delayed-delivery E2Es; link removal coverage to R1-q16 F.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-8-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-9-4. **Medium — FR-011, AC-012/013/044: late 
completions remain untested.** AC-044 pauses before dispatch; AC-013 stops drains but never releases a late 
success/error afterward. Existing completions write to conversation-only cache keys 
([useMessages.ts:317](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/useMessages.ts:317)). 
[SPEC:275](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:275). **Fix:** add E2Es 
releasing real create and lookup responses after A→C and confirmed logout. Assert no old content enters C’s view, no 
deleted item reappears, and stale completions cannot modify replacement claims. **r2 #6 remains partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-10-
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-12-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-13-6. **Medium — G2, FR-001/002, 
AC-005/038/040: pending-to-stored UI correlation is unspecified.** Current message types/mappers omit 
`clientMessageId`; optimistic matching guesses from content and timestamps within one second 
([message-cache.ts:28](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/message-cache.ts:28)). That cannot reliably 
reconcile long-queued or identical messages before the HTTP response arrives. 
[SPEC:93](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:93). **Fix:** require stable 
key-based correlation across outbox, create, lookup, feed, and Realtime representations. Test identical text with 
different reply/mention compositions, Realtime-before-response, and one bubble throughout in both sender tabs.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-14-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md:15:7. **Medium — FR-027/028, AC-028/029: 
metrics bounds regressed and hanging delivery is insufficiently bounded.** V1 explicitly bounded request size and 
batch length ([SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews
/SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205)); v2 retains only field bounds, a client buffer, and request-rate limiting. One enormous 
valid batch can flood logs. Repeated hanging batches can accumulate outside the buffer and consume HTTP capacity. 
[SPEC:119](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:119). **Fix:** restore 
byte/event-count limits; define bounded concurrent delivery, cancellation deadlines, and overload dropping. Test 
oversized valid batches and sustained hanging traffic while messaging continues. **r2 #14 remains partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-16-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-17-8. **Medium — FR-008, AC-009, §12: 
quota-free replay lacks an independent abuse budget and concurrent charging rule.** Exact replay performs 
authenticated database reads/enrichment 
([create/route.ts:336](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts:336)). Unlimited replay/lookup 
traffic can bypass the create quota. Concurrent requests for an initially absent key can also be charged before 
becoming replays. [SPEC:100](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:100). 
**Fix:** preserve D1’s exemption while adding a separate shared request budget for replay/lookup traffic. Charge 
create quota only once for the winning insertion. Test concurrent same-key requests and concurrent distinct keys at 
the quota boundary.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r3.md-18-
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-2-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-3-1. **High — Degraded mode still permits 
loss.** FR-001/033, AC-039 
([SPEC:125](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:125)). Unpersisted sends 
remain allowed. Closing the drawer or changing its view unmounts the composer without a browser unload warning; its 
text and key are component state 
([composer:133](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/message-composer.tsx:133), 
[drawer:279](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/MessagingDrawer.tsx:279)). This contradicts R1-q2 A 
and leaves r2 #1/r3 #2 open. **Fix:** “If persistence fails, do not dispatch; show an actionable storage failure and 
retain the composition.” AC-039 must assert zero create requests.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-4-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md:5:2. **High — Stale fences and completions 
lack protection under the same identity.** FR-004/006/011, AC-045/047 
([SPEC:98](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:98)). Fencing is described 
by message key, while completion invalidation is triggered by account changes. A delayed fence can arrive after lease 
takeover and revoke a newer attempt; a delayed original request can arrive after cancellation. AC-045 tests only an 
INSERT already blocked inside Postgres. The existing create path separates lookup and insertion ([repository:530](/E:/p
rojects/virtual-office/src/repositories/implementations/supabase/SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:530)). **Fix:** require 
attempt/claim generations on mutations and completions, reject revoked generations, and test delayed pre-registration 
creates plus stale fences after takeover.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-6-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-7-3. **High — Notification authorization can 
return a stale positive result.** FR-025, BR-011, AC-049 
([SPEC:117](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:117)). Authorize B, hold 
the positive response, remove B while Realtime is blocked, then release it: the last completed check still says 
“member.” Holding the request before authorization does not test this race. Literal membership at browser emission 
cannot be guaranteed by a prior server read. **Fix:** define the authorization boundary explicitly, require final 
identity/revocation checks without intervening awaits, and obtain owner acceptance of any remaining check-to-display 
race. AC-049 must hold an already-positive response.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-8-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md:9:4. **Medium — Lease recovery contradicts 
D1’s delivery deadline.** FR-002/004, AC-041 
([SPEC:96](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:96)). Connectivity can 
return with one pending item and available quota while its hung owner retains a 30/45-second claim. Another tab cannot 
deliver within ten seconds under the stated rules. **Fix:** specify immediate, safely fenced recovery on connectivity 
return rather than waiting for that lease; distinguish commit-capable attempts from lingering transport requests. Add 
this D1 scenario to acceptance coverage.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-10-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-11-5. **Medium — D3’s ordinary-client 
revocation requirement is weakened.** FR-019/BR-009 says “as soon as it learns,” without requiring timely removal 
detection ([SPEC:111](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:111)); D3 says 
the ordinary app removes the member immediately 
([state:221](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/state.md:221)). The current 
conversation subscription does not observe membership rows 
([subscription:18](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/realtime/useConversationRealtime.ts:18)). Cached Realtime 
authorization also affects sending, while the documented residual discusses receipt. [Supabase 
authorization](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization#updating-rls-policies). **Fix:** require 
removal detection independent of continued conversation access, enforce current-member publishing, and test a removed 
client that stays subscribed and attempts to send.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-12-
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-14-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-15-7. **Medium — Winning-insert charging 
leaves unsuccessful create traffic unbudgeted.** FR-008 and §12 
([SPEC:100](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:100)). Distinct-key 
requests rejected for invalid replies or exhausted quota are neither winning inserts nor stored-message replays. They 
can perform unlimited authenticated database work under the stated budgets. Currently they encounter the request quota 
before reply validation ([create:272](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts:272)). **Fix:** 
require an independent request budget covering all create attempts, including validation failures and quota losers; 
preserve D1’s exemption from the insertion quota.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-16-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md:17:8. **Medium — Expired manual retry has 
contradictory retry rules.** FR-008/009, BR-006, AC-010 
([SPEC:101](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:101)). After manual retry 
receives 429, FR-008 requires automatic retry, but the unchanged item remains older than 24 hours and FR-009 prohibits 
automatic sending. **Fix:** explicitly define a renewed delivery window upon manual retry, retaining the key and 
original timestamp for metrics. Test manual retry followed by 429 and an unknown outcome.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-18-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-19-9. **Medium — Acceptance coverage still 
overstates traceability.** AC-024/029/044/046 and §15 
([SPEC:294](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:294)):
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews/sol-review-spec-r4.md-20-   - AC-044 covers sender mismatch, not 
anon access or another user’s key under the caller’s own identity.
  98: ## Round 1 answers (user, 2026-10-06; option labels from round-1.html)
  99: 
 100: - R1-q1 Must items: R1 offline queue, R2 Realtime reconnect incl. conversation
 101:   list, R3 polling fallback >30s, R4 reliable typing, R5 live cross-device
 102:   unread/read sync, R7 @mention desktop notifications. R6 metrics NOT selected.
 103: - R1-q2 "reliable" = A no message silently lost (delivers or visible failure
 104:   with action); B never duplicates (auto-resend, several tabs); C pending
 105:   messages deliver within ~10 s after connectivity returns without clicks;
 106:   D with Realtime down, others' new messages appear within ~30–45 s via
 107:   polling; E offline-sent order preserved.
 108: - R1-q3 A: queue in IndexedDB per user; survives reload/close; deleted on logout.
 109: - R1-q4 A: queue only text + replies; attachments/voice offline keep the
 110:   Phase 4 failure-in-composer + "Tentar de novo".
 111: - R1-q5 A in order, one at a time per conversation, later ones wait if one
 112:   fails; B pending shown in feed with clock state, cancellable before sending;
 113:   C definitive rejection (lost access, invalid content, rate limit) stops
 114:   retrying, shows failure with text preserved; D pending expires after a time
 115:   (example 24 h) and becomes a visible failure without auto-send. E (edit
 116:   pending) not selected.
 117: - R1-q6 A: discreet banner at the top of the chat ("Sem conexão — mensagens
 118:   serão enviadas quando voltar" / "Reconectando…"), hides itself when normal.
 119: - R1-q7 A: poll every 15 s, only while tab visible: open conversation +
 120:   conversation list (unread); stops as soon as Realtime returns.
 121: - R1-q8 A keeps showing during continuous typing, disappears ~5 s after stop;
 122:   B names ("Ana está digitando…", "Ana e Bruno…", "3 pessoas…"); C DM, group,
 123:   room; D private channel, only conversation members receive typing; E never
 124:   show my own typing from my other tabs/devices.
 125: - R1-q9 A unread counter + read state sync live across my devices; B messages
 126:   I sent from another device appear immediately. C stars, D drafts, E
 127:   cross-device notification dismissal NOT selected.
 128: - R1-q10 A typing @ opens member list of the conversation, choosing inserts a
 129:   highlighted mention; B mentioned user gets desktop notification even in a
 130:   ROOM; E mention valid only for conversation members, otherwise plain text.
 131:   C (notify even with DM/group notifications off) and D (@todos/@here) NOT
 132:   selected.
 133: - R1-q11 A: background = tab open but hidden/minimized (Phase 4 model); no
 134:   service worker / Web Push.
 135: - R1-q12 B: metrics, if included, as technical logs only (Supabase/Vercel), no
 136:   UI. (Conflicts with R1-q1 not selecting R6 → asked in round 2.)
 137: - R1-q13 A: migrations local during the phase; online at phase end with
 138:   explicit authorization; app deployment stays with the user.
 139: - R1-q14 A Chrome + Edge desktop (automated), B Firefox desktop. Safari and
 140:   mobile NOT selected.
 141: - R1-q15 Phase 4 follow-ups in scope: A DB — membership check in
 142:   mark_conversation_read and block anon from get_unread_counts; C restore the
 143:   open conversation after page reload. B, D, E, F not selected.
 144: - R1-q16 Must never happen: A one user's pending message sent by another user
 145:   who later logs in on the same browser; B duplicates when two tabs drain the
 146:   same queue; C notification for my own message or the conversation I'm
 147:   viewing; D polling continuing after Realtime returned; E typing stuck after
 148:   the person left/closed the tab; F mention notifying a non-member.
 149: - R1-q17 A: acceptance like Phase 4 — two-account E2E (simulated internet and
 150:   Realtime outages) + local DB integration tests + owner final test against the
 151:   online DB. (Repo policy: no unit tests.)
 152: - R1-q18 A: all company members who use chat (DM, group, room); no admin
 153:   specifics except possibly metrics.
