45:## T28 — Membership integrity: memberships only through authorized server paths
47:Task: A `conversation_members` row is created or restored only by a server path that authorizes that user for that 
conversation (direct conversation creation among the users it names, under the existing company rules; room 
conversation membership per the room's access rules; an explicitly authorized room join/rejoin; test seeding). No anon 
or authenticated client — acting through `conversation_members`, `conversations` INSERT/UPDATE (`participants`, 
`room_id`, `type`), the participant sync trigger `sync_conversation_members`, the conversation resolver/join routes, 
or any other RPC, view, or trigger — can make itself or any other user a member it is not authorized to be, or move a 
membership to another conversation or user. A removed membership stays removed when unrelated writes happen (another 
user's join, a participants sync, preference/archive/read writes); only an authorized rejoin restores it. Preference, 
archive, and read writes update an existing membership and never create one; a membership that vanished between 
authorization and the write is answered as not a participant with no row created. What a client DELETE of its own 
membership means (leave, or forbidden) is decided and recorded. The hosted build and the Phase 4 build keep creating 
direct and room conversations, joining rooms, and changing preferences/archive/read state (including their user-scoped 
writes, e.g. preference upserts of an existing membership). The inventory of membership writers and the decision for 
each is recorded in TRACK.
48:Done when: On the local database, for each inventoried path, neither a hostile actor nor the user it targets gains 
or regains membership without authorization, and the legitimate creation, join, rejoin, preference, archive, and read 
flows of the current, Phase 4, and hosted builds still work.
49:Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests (PostgREST as anon, as an authenticated outsider, and as a current 
member; real routes) asserting the complete membership delta and the affected users' access (403 on 
create/fence/roster, no messages/mentions): own INSERT into another conversation; UPDATE moving a row to another 
conversation/user; a member adding an outsider through `participants`; conversation INSERT naming 
arbitrary/cross-company participants or an unauthorized private room; `room_id`/`type` retargeting followed by 
resolver/join calls; removal → another user's legitimate join → removed user still denied, then an authorized rejoin 
restores access; preference and archive mutations held after authorization, membership deleted, then released → no 
replacement row and access still denied; legitimate flows and old-build contracts (user-scoped conversation creation, 
preference/archive upserts of an existing membership) still pass; `npm run test:messaging:local:e2e` passes; 
presence-safety reviewer and the Presence DB suite run if any room/Presence/Knock path is touched; RLS review gate 
recorded.
56:Task: A private Realtime topic per conversation whose join and broadcast send are authorized only for current 
members (`users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text` → `users.id` membership); anon clients, authenticated non-members, 
and the public topic name receive no typing events and cannot send events members receive; existing private topics 
(Presence, screen share) are unaffected.
108:## T27 — Unknown-outcome recovery through the fence
110:Task: An attempt that ends without a usable response (network error after dispatch, timeout, 5xx after reaching 
the server, tab closed mid-request) leaves the item unknown; before any cancel, expiry, or redispatch the app fences 
it under a new generation; a stored result resolves as delivered (never cancelled or expired); a not-stored result 
only permits the transition that was requested — cancel and expiry complete without any create, and redispatch happens 
only while the item is still current, eligible, and inside its delivery window; cancel is offered only for items known 
not stored; a fence answered 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (access lost while the item was unknown) makes the item failed per 
BR-005 with its text kept, stops automatic attempts, and is never treated as not stored (no expiry, no cancel) — 
"Tentar de novo" fences under a new generation first, so a stored result resolves as delivered and a not-stored result 
follows the normal rules, and "Apagar" only removes the local item.
111:Done when: AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, and the AC-046 5xx clause hold in the real UI with real routes, an 
unknown item fenced as not stored after its 24 h window expires without any create request, and an unknown item whose 
fence returns 403 is failed (not expired, not delivered, not re-created) for both a committed-but-response-lost 
message and a not-yet-stored one.
121:Verify by: New E2E specs (two tabs, held create, tab close, hung lease, attempt dispatched during outage, 
simultaneous online, cancel/claim race, network-log overlap check) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; 
regression suites pass.
126:## T9 — Definitive failures, rate-limit retry, and expiry
128:Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only later 
items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under a new 
key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry automatically in order; items fenced as not stored 24 
h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not stored" — 
T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the original send time and opens a new 24 h window under the 
normal rules.
